WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.367
Welcome to the training academy.

2
00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:14.733
This lesson helps the Customer Champion lead implementation efficiently, without scheduling multiple training calls.

3
00:00:14.733 --> 00:00:22.100
The aim is to prepare one small team, demonstrate one complete route day, and enter the readiness review with evidence, not unanswered setup questions.

4
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:30.700
The Customer Champion must be an Owner or Admin.

5
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:39.300
They coordinate the implementation calendar, verify the data file, assign user roles, ensure the Dispatcher and pilot Driver complete their training, and own the customer signoff.

6
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:47.900
The onboarding program provides the Academy, launch docket, product support, and a focused thirty minute readiness review.

7
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:53.120
Follow the seven day rhythm in the launch docket.

8
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.340
On day one, confirm the Champion, users, depot, and support path.

9
00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:03.560
On day two, prepare the pilot driver, vehicle, customers, and route file.

10
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:08.780
On days three and four, import, validate, optimize, and review blockers.

11
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:14.000
On days five and six, run the practice route, capture proof, and rehearse an exception.

12
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:22.133
Keep the first implementation narrow.

13
00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:30.267
One depot, one Dispatcher, one Driver, one ready vehicle, and one representative route day are sufficient.

14
00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:38.400
A small scope aids in identifying issues like a bad address, missing capacity rule, access problem, or confusing status transition before expanding the system to more routes.

15
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:51.675
The standard onboarding package includes Academy access, the Customer Launch Docket, best effort support with a one business day initial response target, and one thirty minute launch readiness review.

16
00:01:51.675 --> 00:02:04.950
Additional services like customer data cleanup, custom integrations, onsite work, live team training, and customer specific process design are separately scoped.

17
00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:12.033
After this lesson, open Settings and confirm the customer Champion, the Dispatcher, the pilot Driver, and the escalation contact.

18
00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:19.117
Then complete the knowledge check.

19
00:02:19.117 --> 00:02:26.200
Your progress is saved to the organization, and the readiness card will guide you to the next incomplete training or workspace step.

20
00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:33.688
Before proceeding, open the launch docket and note down the Champion, Dispatcher, pilot Driver, target practice date, and escalation contact.

21
00:02:33.688 --> 00:02:41.175
Ensure everyone understands the self guided model and the boundary between included support and separately scoped services.

22
00:02:41.175 --> 00:02:48.663
If any owner is missing, pause here and assign one.

23
00:02:48.663 --> 00:02:56.150
Clear ownership now prevents the readiness review from becoming a basic setup meeting later.
